ers based on spending thresholds\n\n3. **Performance Results**:\n   - Baseline (P0): 0.13423 (1-auroc)\n   - Best Score Achieved: 0.09012 (1-auroc) \n   - Improvement: ~33% reduction in error\n\n## Why These Changes Worked\n\n- The engineered features capture meaningful patterns in customer behavior\n- Log transformations helped with skewed distributions\n- Interaction terms captured complex relationships between variables\n- Time-based features (days since registration) provided temporal context\n- Spending ratios normalized the data and made comparisons meaningful\n- The combination of spending, purchasing, and demographic features created a rich representation that the frozen model could leverage effectively"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":24669,"output":396,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25065,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790971459279,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8b6117676f6d6ef0","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_bd9452ad3fda45d1a8d308c7","toolName":"write","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Successfully wrote to NOTES.md"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790971461428},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_73aaa7e89b23412eb80cc42c","name":"bash","arguments":{"command":"tabfm-eval"}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":25084,"output":25,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25109,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"toolUse","timestamp":1790971461430,"responseId":"chatcmpl-8da047b438136f28","rawStopReason":"tool_calls","thinkingLevel":"off"},{"role":"toolResult","toolCallId":"call_73aaa7e89b23412eb80cc42c","toolName":"bash","content":[{"type":"text","text":"eval #8: 1-auroc = 0.09060 (+/- 0.0176 over 3 folds) \n  features=42 views=1 time=6.75s | P0=0.13423 best_before=0.09012\n  secondary: logloss=0.2546, acc=0.8955, auroc=0.9094, 1-auroc=0.0906\n  budget: 8/16 evaluations used\n"}],"isError":false,"timestamp":1790971469462},{"role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"Our best result so far is 0.09012 (achieved in eval #3), which represents a significant improvement over the baseline of 0.13423. Let me finalize our best pipeline and document our approach:\n\n"},{"type":"toolCall","id":"call_7ed2ee5b00974bf4a3848634","name":"write","arguments":{"path":"FINAL_PIPELINE.md","content":"# Final Pipeline for Marketing Campaign Dataset\n\nThis pipeline achieved the best score of 1-auroc = 0.09012 (eval #3) on the Marketing Campaign dataset.\n\n## Key Features Implemented\n\n1. **Data Preprocessing**:\n   - Fill missing Income values with median\n   - Proper handling of datetime features\n\n2. **Feature Engineering**:\n   - Customer age calculation from birth year\n   - Days since customer registration\n   - Total spending from multiple product categories\n   - Spending ratios (particularly Wine spending ratio)\n   - Purchase frequency metrics\n   - Deal engagement rate\n   - Interaction features (Income × Age, Income × Spending)\n   - Log transformation for skewed features\n   - Family size aggregation\n   - High-value customer identification\n\n## Why This Works Well\n\nThe engineered features capture important behavioral patterns:\n- Temporal aspects (days since registration)\n- Spending behaviors (total spending, ratios)\n- Purchase patterns (frequency, engagement)\n- Demographic relationships (age, income)\n- Product preferences (spending categories)\n\nThis combination provides rich, informative features that the frozen TabPFN model can effectively utilize for binary classification."}}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":25249,"output":317,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrit