das, numpy, and scikit-learn transforms as required. The frozen model remains unchanged, and all improvements come from better data preparation and feature engineering.\n\nThe approach focused on creating interpretable, domain-relevant features that help the TabPFN model distinguish between customers who responded to marketing campaigns versus those who didn't, ultimately achieving a 33% improvement over the baseline score.\n"}],"api":"openai-completions","provider":"vllm","model":"Qwen/Qwen3-Coder-30B-A3B-Instruct","usage":{"input":25586,"output":364,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"reasoning":0,"totalTokens":25950,"cost":{"input":0,"output":0,"cacheRead":0,"cacheWrite":0,"total":0}},"stopReason":"stop","timestamp":1790971471213,"responseId":"chatcmpl-b7e53eedc350743a","rawStopReason":"stop","thinkingLevel":"off"}],"willRetry":false}
